lines[12]:
  - i, text, start, end
  - 0, What would you do if the power went out for three whole days?, 0.35, 3.073
  - 1, "It's nine at night, and suddenly everything goes dark.", 3.333, 6.141
  - 2, Step one: don't touch the fridge., 6.401, 7.981
  - 3, "If you keep it closed, your food stays cold for about four hours, and a full freezer lasts two days.", 8.241, 13.718
  - 4, "Step two: grab a flashlight, not a candle.", 13.978, 15.952
  - 5, Candles and dark rooms are a real fire risk., 16.212, 18.678
  - 6, "Step three: fill some bottles with water,", 18.938, 21.038
  - 7, "about a gallon per person, every day.", 21.178, 23.121
  - 8, "Step four: unplug your electronics,", 23.381, 25.337
  - 9, "because when the power comes back, a surge can fry them.", 25.337, 28.248
  - 10, Day three: the lights flicker back on., 28.508, 30.28
  - 11, "And because you were ready, you're totally fine.", 30.54, 32.573
